WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.460
- [Lex] Can you just touch

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.560
on the topic of simulation?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.350
Do you find this thought
experiment that we're living

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.650
in a simulation useful,
inspiring or constructive

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.710
in any kind of way?

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.110
Do you think it's ridiculous?

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.130
Do you think it could be true?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.650
Or is it just a useful thought experiment?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.050
- I think it is extremely
useful as a thought experiment

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.840
because it makes sense to everyone,

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.650
especially as we see virtual
reality and computer games

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.740
getting more and more complex.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.010
You're not talking to an
audience in Newton's time

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.697
where you're like "Imagine a
clock that it has mechanics

00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:42.370
"in it that are so complex
that it can create love."

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.470
And everyone's like "Mmmm, no."

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.303
(interviewer laughing)

00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:48.690
But today you really start to feel, man,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.110
at point is this little
robot friend of mine

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:56.110
gonna be like someone I don't
want to cancel plans with.

00:00:56.876 --> 00:00:58.160
(laughs)

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.170
And so it's a great,
the thought experiment

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.660
of do we live in a simulation,
am a a brain in a vat

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.330
that has just been given
electrical impulses

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:12.140
from some nefarious other
beings so that I believe

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.240
that I live on earth and that
I have a body and all of this.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.660
And the fact that you
can't prove it either way

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.670
is a fantastic way to introduce people

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.593
to some of the deepest questions.

